# metrics-dashboard.ine — an operations metrics dashboard written with ONLY
# the current dictionary vocabulary (page, header, logo, navigation,
# container, card-group, card, section, button, footer, title/text).
#
# Evidence-collection experiment (PLAN mission 72): feed the typed-value
# (number / boolean / date) type-system decision with real-program data.
# A metrics dashboard needs currency and percentage formatting, enabled/
# disabled states, and timestamp display; this program shows what that
# intent reduces to when the only value a property can carry is text.
# Every line the vocabulary could not guide is flagged with `vocab gap:`
# and listed in .agent/NOTES.md ("## Mission 72").

make page
page title "Metrics Dashboard"

make header
header inside page
make logo
logo text "Acme Ops"
logo inside header
make navigation
navigation inside header

# KPI row. Numbers lex and parse as NUMBER tokens (the pipeline stores real
# int/float values), but the dictionary declares `text`/`title` as text
# values and the HTML backend prints them through str() with no formatting:
# no thousands separator, no percent sign, no currency prefix, no locale.
make kpi-rows container
kpi-rows inside page
make metrics card-group
metrics inside kpi-rows
make 4 card
group kpis = card-1 card-2 card-3 card-4
kpis inside metrics
card-1 title "Revenue"
card-1 text 1234567.89
# vocab gap: the value is a bare number, yet the program MEANS a currency
# amount. There is no number type tracked by the dictionary and no format
# intent (currency/locale/precision), so the reader cannot know it should
# render as $1,234,567.89; the author must pre-format the string instead,
# which turns the value into opaque text (unusable for math, sorting, or a
# chart). `value_shape("card","text")` is "text", so the editor offers a
# quoted-string snippet — never a numeric placeholder.

card-2 title "Uptime"
card-2 text 99.98
# vocab gap: the 99.98 is a percentage by convention only — no unit, no
# percent type, no decimal-count control. As a bare string the renderer
# prints 99.98 and cannot append the "%" consistently across cards.

card-3 title "Workload"
card-3 text 42
# vocab gap: an integer with no declared type. Two KPIs on the same
# dashboard render identically even though one means 42.0% and the other
# means 1234567.89 (a currency); the distinction lives only in the author's
# head, as a pre-formatted string convention.

card-4 title "Queued jobs"
card-4 text "0 of 12"
# vocab gap: a string-concatenated ratio. "0 of 12" cannot be sorted or
# graphed; a real typed pair (0, 12) would render differently and stay
# computable. String concatenation is the ONLY tool today, and it hard-codes
# the display format into the source.

# Status panel: an enabled/disabled boolean is inexpressible. Because `make N
# <kind>` restarts numbering from 1 per statement, the second batch needs
# explicit names (same collision Mission 55 documented).
make status-panel container
status-panel inside page
make flags card-group
flags inside status-panel
make gate-1 card
make gate-2 card
make gate-3 card
group toggles = gate-1 gate-2 gate-3
toggles inside flags
gate-1 title "Feature flags"
gate-1 text "enabled"
gate-2 title "Maintenance mode"
gate-2 text "disabled"
gate-3 title "Read replica"
gate-3 text "degraded"
# vocab gap: "enabled" / "disabled" / "degraded" are display strings, not
# boolean or enumerated state. There is no boolean value (button.interactive
# already documents: "not settable yet: Ine has no boolean values"), so
# nothing can toggle, and no state color/icon can be derived from a word.
# A boolean would also give the backend a truth value to branch on — a
# string cannot.

# Timestamp panel: dates are strings with no format or timezone.
make deploy-panel container
deploy-panel inside page
make deploys card-group
deploys inside deploy-panel
make dep-1 card
make dep-2 card
make dep-3 card
group releases = dep-1 dep-2 dep-3
releases inside deploys
dep-1 title "v2.14"
dep-1 text "2026-09-17 12:40 UTC"
dep-2 title "v2.13"
dep-2 text "2026-09-16 09:15 UTC"
dep-3 title "v2.12"
dep-3 text "2026-09-15 22:03 UTC"
# vocab gap: three timestamps as literal strings. No date type means no
# "3h ago" rendering, no sortable comparison, no timezone math, and no
# validation (the strings exist as atoms; a typo is invisible to the
# language).

# The footer carries a relative-time string, baked in at authoring time.
make footer
footer text "Last synced 2 minutes ago"
footer inside page
# vocab gap: relative time is baked into the text; no runtime can recompute
# it, because there is no timestamp value to diff.

say page title
say card-1 text
say card-2 text
say 42